# Merge policy for the repo's hottest file (airhorn-tp3g).
#
# tools/suite-map.tsv is the map the fast gate reads: a changed path -> the suites that cover it. It is a SET
# that the gate unions at run time, so two branches adding rows for different files are both right and only
# the TEXT merge fails. This attribute hands the file to a union driver instead.
#
# A .gitattributes entry alone does NOT configure a driver - git will not run a driver that comes from the
# repository itself - so each clone opts in ONCE, and without that config the ordinary text merge runs and
# conflicts loudly (the safe failure, never a silent no-op):
#
#   git config merge.suite-map-union.driver "node tools/merge-suite-map.mjs --driver %O %A %B"
#   git config merge.suite-map-union.name "union tools/suite-map.tsv by key"
#
# The manual path needs no configuration at all and always works mid-conflict. Pass the merge BASE (:1:) as
# the third file: with it the merge is THREE-WAY, so a row - or a comment block - that one side DELETED is
# deleted, instead of being put back by an additive union (airhorn-famo: 47 deleted self-rows came back that
# way, exit 0, looking like a clean merge). Without a base the tool keeps every row either side has and REFUSES
# a one-side-only self-row by name, because there it cannot tell "added" from "deleted".
#
#   git show :1:tools/suite-map.tsv > /tmp/base.tsv
#   git show :2:tools/suite-map.tsv > /tmp/ours.tsv
#   git show :3:tools/suite-map.tsv > /tmp/theirs.tsv
#   node tools/merge-suite-map.mjs --union /tmp/ours.tsv /tmp/theirs.tsv /tmp/base.tsv --write tools/suite-map.tsv
#   node tools/derive-coverage-contract.mjs          # the contract is DERIVED: never merge it, regenerate it
#   git add tools/suite-map.tsv .fleet/coverage-contract.json
#
# The second line is not optional: the map and .fleet/coverage-contract.json move together, which is why the
# 20:14Z collision aborted on both files. A union without the regenerate step resolves the conflict and then
# fails tests/gate-map.test.js on a stale contract - loudly, which is the point, but do it in one go.
#
# Either way a disagreement (an "!" exemption on one side and a real row on the other, a truncated row, a
# malformed line, a row deleted on one side and changed on the other) FAILS LOUDLY rather than being resolved
# by preference. tests/suite-map-merge.test.js pins this file, the driver's three-way merge, and the loud
# failures.

tools/suite-map.tsv merge=suite-map-union
